# Optional connection invitations without a note
Workstream-ID: lea-31
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/31
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded connection-invitation fallback
Status: BLOCKED
Blocked-stage: Ready
Blocker: Await a coordinated save point before replacing source used by an independent application.
Milestone: Offer an explicit fallback when connection notes are unavailable
Dependencies: lea-11

## Purpose
Allow an optional plain connection invitation when the invitation dialog cannot
offer a note. Keep the existing note-first behavior and require an explicit
opt-in rather than silently sending invitations without their drafted notes.

## Tasks
- [x] Trace connector, configuration, desktop, persistence and reporting boundaries.
- [x] Establish an isolated fictional development lane and preservation baseline.
- [x] Add an off-by-default setting and desktop toggle with two-line hover help.
- [x] Implement a guarded note-free send path without weakening dry-run or limits.
- [x] Persist and display invitation delivery separately from actual note delivery.
- [x] Qualify affected behavior offline and update directly affected guides.
- [x] Retain one existing issue-backed Project item and persistent backlink.
- [x] Integrate and qualify the combined, separately authorized source-publication lane.
- [ ] Promote the complete qualified candidate at a coordinated source-app save point.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Existing configurations continue to require a connection note by default.
- [x] When available, the drafted note is preferred even with fallback enabled.
- [x] An unavailable note can use only a positively identified invitation send action.
- [x] Dry-run never sends, unavailable controls fail explicitly and weekly limits stop.
- [x] Successful plain invitations count as invitations, not delivered notes.
- [x] Persistence prevents repeated invitations and leaves the full message pending.
- [x] Desktop overrides preserve saved configuration and describe the fallback clearly.
- [x] Fictional checks preserve private inputs, running applications and released assets.
- [x] Technical completion is distinguished from live qualification and publication.
- [x] One issue-backed Project item and a durable backlink represent this workstream.
- [ ] Source promotion is verified without disrupting the independent application.

## Completion evidence
Implementation and technical qualification are complete in isolated public
source. The active original checkout and installed v0.2.3 do not contain this
update. Updating that checkout remains blocked to protect an independently
running application. Separate source publication does not activate that app;
a different port or a passing fixture is not isolation.

The off-by-default setting and Behavior checkbox prefer an available note.
Fallback requires a visible, enabled, explicitly identified Send without a note
button inside the invitation dialog. Hidden, disabled and misleading controls
do not authorize sending; arbitrary note-send failures do not downgrade.

Separate invitation and note timestamps prevent repeated pending invitations
without falsely marking a draft delivered. Plain invitations retain both drafts,
leave overdue invitation priority and are reported separately from sent notes
and full hiring-team messages. Legacy note-only rows remain recognized.

All 238 affected regression cases pass. Black/Ruff pass thirteen changed Python
files and mypy passes seventy-three implementation files. Twelve actual offline
browser scenarios pass, including note preference, dry-run, control identity and
weekly-limit boundaries. Both fictional native themes are checked and visually
reviewed with the complete toggle label visible. Eight affected guides describe
the candidate separately from the released executable.

Auxiliary browser routing, scroll geometry and missing-font assumptions initially
failed. Correct the private checker using the existing font-registration helper
rather than weakening product checks. No live LinkedIn qualification, human
acceptance, source activation or independent restart is claimed by these checks.

The separately authorized source-publication lane integrates all twenty-nine
combined no-note and Windows-branding payloads. Both overlapping files merge
cleanly; all twenty-seven nonoverlapping payloads match the frozen candidates
exactly. All 253 combined affected cases pass; repository Ruff, Black over
119 files and mypy over seventy-three implementation modules pass. Preserve
the original frozen evidence. Commit/remote/hosted qualification read-back is
a separate publication gate, not evidence that the active checkout switched.
No new tag, release, installer replacement or live LinkedIn action is included.

